{"timestamp": 1779395918.56963, "event_type": "meeting_called", "tick": 27, "data": {"caller": "player_1", "reason": "Bob called an emergency meeting", "bodies": [{"room": "upper_engine", "victim_name": "Diana"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779395918.5701172, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 27, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779395930.686982, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 27, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I called this because I found Diana\u2019s body in upper_engine. My route was lower_engine -> upper_engine -> medbay -> electrical -> cafeteria. The only player I saw this round was Frank, and I saw him in upper_engine around tick 9, which is where Diana\u2019s body was. I\u2019m not hard accusing yet, but Frank is the only person I can place near the body."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395955.2326012, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 27, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I\u2019ll share what I have: my route was upper_engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation. I didn\u2019t encounter anyone at all this round, and I didn\u2019t see Diana\u2019s body when I was in upper_engine, so if she died there it was after I left.\n\nBob, one thing that worries me is you said you \u201cfound Diana\u2019s body in upper_engine\u201d but this is an emergency meeting, not a body report. If you were actually on the body, why not report it immediately? That feels like an important detail.\n\nRight now the only claimed sighting is Bob placing Frank in upper_engine, but we need to hear Frank\u2019s route and explanation before deciding. At 3 alive we really can\u2019t afford a bad vote or a skip if we have enough evidence."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395968.7143838, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 27, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Bob, you are 100% the Duck. Your story completely falls apart. \n\nFirst off, you claim you saw me in upper_engine around tick 9. That is completely impossible. My route was weapons -> security -> navigation early on, so I was on the complete opposite side of the map at that time. I only came up the left side (storage -> lower_engine -> upper_engine -> oxygen) at the very end of the round. \n\nSecond, Eve's point is the absolute nail in the coffin. You claim you found Diana's body in upper_engine, yet you ran all the way to the cafeteria to press the emergency button instead of just reporting the body right there? The only reason you do that is if you killed her yourself and either had a cooldown or wanted to try and control the narrative by calling a meeting. \n\nYou're lying about seeing me to frame me because you're caught. Eve, we vote Bob here and win. I'm voting Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395994.721667, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 27, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Let me clarify the emergency/report point because I get why that sounds bad: I did not report from upper_engine, I hit the cafeteria button. My wording of \u201cfound Diana\u2019s body\u201d was sloppy \u2014 the important part is I saw Frank in upper_engine around tick 9, and now Diana is dead.\n\nFrank\u2019s route claim doesn\u2019t match what I saw. I was in upper_engine and saw Frank there. He\u2019s saying he was on the complete opposite side at that time, but that\u2019s just false from my POV.\n\nEve, from your route, you left upper_engine early and didn\u2019t see a body. That means Diana likely died after you left. The only person I can place in upper_engine after that is Frank. Frank is trying to make this about the emergency button wording because he can\u2019t explain why I saw him there.\n\nI\u2019m voting Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779396021.8025641, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 27, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I\u2019m still leaning Bob here because the story keeps changing in a way that matters.\n\nMy info is unchanged: I started in upper_engine, then went oxygen \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation. I saw nobody and I did not see Diana\u2019s body in upper_engine when I was there, so she died after I left.\n\nThe biggest issue is Bob first said he found Diana\u2019s body in upper_engine, but this was an emergency button from cafeteria, not a report. Now he\u2019s saying the wording was sloppy and the main point is that he saw Frank there. But if he didn\u2019t actually see the body, then how is he so sure Diana died in upper_engine? And if he did see the body, leaving it to go hit button is very suspicious.\n\nFrank\u2019s defense is at least directly addressing the accusation and points out that inconsistency. Bob\u2019s case is basically only \u201cI saw Frank,\u201d with no one else able to confirm it. Since we\u2019re at final three, I think the safer vote is Bob unless something major changes."}}
